Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dpu: skip command commit waits before enabling

msm_atomic_commit_tail() waits for the preceding flush before modeset enable.
On an off-to-on transition the new CRTC state is active but the physical
encoder remains disabled. Return the already-supported -EWOULDBLOCK before
reading CTL state or entering the IRQ helper. Keep enabled-encoder waits and
the helper's unexpected-disabled diagnostic unchanged.

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/dpu1/dpu_encoder_phys_cmd.c
@@ -683,6 +683,10 @@
 static int dpu_encoder_phys_cmd_wait_for_commit_done(
 		struct dpu_encoder_phys *phys_enc)
 {
+	/* The pre-enable wait_flush has no previous commit to wait for. */
+	if (phys_enc->enable_state == DPU_ENC_DISABLED)
+		return -EWOULDBLOCK;
+
 	/* only required for master controller */
 	if (!dpu_encoder_phys_cmd_is_master(phys_enc))
 		return 0;
